{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread","id":666688,"title":"The Otherkin Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-16T04:10:46-07:00","id":666688,"title":"The Otherkin Thread","content":"I realized this forum was neglecting a possibly large group of our fellow gamers.<br /> <br /> Otherkin, whether they identify as vampire, lycanthrope, fae, whatever...it deserves attention and a platform for discussion. It means a LOT to the people who live this.<br /> <br /> I'll start with my own really skimpy testimonial (I'll totally answer questions if you're curious. Just don't want to ramble).<br /> <br /> I'm kind of a mutt, as far as Otherkin identity goes. That fits me, though. I've been able to confidently identify as vampyre even before I was able to deal with my bi/pansexuality. I've felt a lycanthropic attraction to the moon for as long as I can remember, and I often feel myself being more beast, animal, monster, than human. I often look at my own hands, expecting to see claws.<br /> This isn't delusion. I know I, a human, don't have claws. I just also FEEL that I ought to. Like they belong on my digits, and that I'm incomplete without them. In my heart, I have wings. <br /> <br /> I'll clarify for those who question the vampyre part. <br /> I feel out of steam a LOT. I've always been able to supplement that by getting some emotional response from someone, or just being close. I realized this mostly wasn't emotional need on my part early on. I just...needed someone. Something. Even an animal to interact with. And I attracted predatory animals like they thought I was going to steal their lunch. I've fed off the tension of staring down a lynx just outside Nogales Arizona in the desert. I could feel it. Eventually it walked away. But I felt it. I'd taken its fight away. Eaten it. It was in me. I was alive.<br /> <br /> As for sanguine feeding, I've done plenty. Feel free to ask if curious. It was nice.<br /> <br /> That seems an adequate introduction.<br /> <br /> \u200bYour turn!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:50:25-07:00","id":667312,"title":"","content":"I think anyone who's ever role-played has felt this a little bit. Otherwise, you'd never feel the urge to pretend to be someone else. I'll come back with my own experiences on this later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:37:46-07:00","id":667460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=667312#post667312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think anyone who's ever role-played has felt this a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly. I dont wanna sound like I'm needlessly deriding these people, but I honestly fail to see how this &quot;Otherkin&quot; business is any different from a mentally askew individual loosing touch with reality and believing himself to be Jesus Christ reborn.<br /> I mean, some of the &quot;Otherkin&quot; people I've seen, has &quot;identified&quot; as a bloody celestial object! A bloody nebulae for goodness sakes!<br /> <br /> I dont think this was the intended purpose of the thread, and if you think this is derailing, you're welcome to ignore me. Otherwise, I'de be happy for some people to justify how this is different from <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">having an undiagnosed mental disorder\u200b or illness. There, fixed that for you. You've been spoken to about this before, watch the choice of language if you wish to keep participating on these forums. If you can't be bothered to show some sensitivity to other forum members don't expect the moderator staff to sit by ignore it.</span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200b This is the last time you will be getting a warning about this, next offense will result in a suspension. Darksider.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-16-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:34:31-07:00","id":667596,"title":"","content":"Krobeles, I'm gonna say to you what I say to people who bitch about transsexual people: What does it matter to you? What about your life changes if someone identifies as a nebula or a vampire or a were-coyote or whatever? What changes in your day-to-day existence except that you have one less reason to assume you know everything about the people you're loking at? Seriously, even if you disagree with how they identify, what do you gain by fighting to enforce your classifications on others except the right to be the barest sliver of an iota more mentally lazy when it comes to categorizing peple according to your perceptions of their traits?<br /> <br /> No one here is looking for your permission to call themselves anything. They're looking for community, for understanding, for self-expression. If the only response you can form to that is to try to tear them down, then please keep it to yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:35:30-07:00","id":667598,"title":"","content":"I don't pretend to understand Otherkin or transgender/transsexual or really anything of that &quot;type&quot;. The closest I've come is (and this is going to sound like I'm pathologising - not my intent, it's just the words I'm used to!), the brain has a kind of 'map' for how the body looks. It's a pretty basic part of our kinesthetic sense. For like 99% of people, this has a pretty close approximation to their actual body, and it all works fairly well.<br /> <br /> For a few people, however, the map is... different, dramatically so. In particularly unfortunate cases, this leads to thinks like body dysmorphic disorder, or even some eating disorders. The theory goes, for that particular sub-&quot;type&quot; of transgender/sexual who want to transition because their body is 'wrong' or whatever, this map is for the 'other' sexed body; breasts, penis, broad shape, whatever. Hence why people among this subtype who do transition tend to feel so much better after, because they're not constantly hitting that confusion where their brain-map and their body are different.<br /> <br /> It's not out of possibility that Otherkin can be thought of as kind of similar, although I suspect to a much lesser degree? Their brain is just wired a little differently, leading to things like Az feeling like they have 'claws'.<br /> <br /> So, they haven't 'lost touch with reality' any more than a person who feels <i>wrong</i> unless they're a particular level of fit, or a homosexual person is attracted to people of the same sex.<br /> <br /> Of course, like I said, I don't really understand, and it's more than likely my whole idea is incredibly offensive, and totally wrong to boot. If so, I apologise, it was not my intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T20:35:30-07:00","id":667749,"title":"","content":"I still believe I'm a god-in-embryo, struggling to break the egg known as reality. Does that count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T21:21:59-07:00","id":667768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=667749#post667749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still believe I'm a god-in-embryo, struggling to break the egg known as reality. Does that count?</div> </div> </div> </div>Close enough for jazz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:24:03-07:00","id":668019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=667596#post667596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Krobeles, I'm gonna say to you what I say to people who bitch about transsexual people: What does it matter to you? What about your life changes if someone identifies as a nebula or a vampire or a were-coyote or whatever? What changes in your day-to-day existence except that you have one less reason to assume you know everything about the people you're loking at? Seriously, even if you disagree with how they identify, what do you gain by fighting to enforce your classifications on others except the right to be the barest sliver of an iota more mentally lazy when it comes to categorizing peple according to your perceptions of their traits?<br /> <br /> No one here is looking for your permission to call themselves anything. They're looking for community, for understanding, for self-expression. If the only response you can form to that is to try to tear them down, then please keep it to yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing. I gain nothing. They're totally free to do and think as they please. I'm not looking to tear anyone down, I am genuinely asking for people to clarify how those two things are different, because I just down see it.<br /> I am not here to give my permission, I'm here to try to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:56:33-07:00","id":668387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=668019#post668019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing. I gain nothing. They're totally free to do and think as they please. I'm not looking to tear anyone down, I am genuinely asking for people to clarify how those two things are different, because I just down see it.<br /> I am not here to give my permission, I'm here to try to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if anyone is going to have the patience to explain it to you. You've already proven to have trouble with things outside your experience, I don't see how this could turn out any different. Maybe you should just chalk this up to &quot;things I don't understand&quot; and walk away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-17-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:22:33-07:00","id":668511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=668387#post668387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if anyone is going to have the patience to explain it to you. You've already proven to have trouble with things outside your experience, I don't see how this could turn out any different. Maybe you should just chalk this up to &quot;things I don't understand&quot; and walk away.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> I've shown an unwillingness to blindly &quot;listen and believe&quot; postulates which aren't supported by solid arguements. It has nothing to do with my experience, but rather with people being unable or unwilling to adequately explain it to me, without taking my disagreement personally.<br /> Also, nice going there, dredging up an old arguement. That was totally nessesary.<br /> <br /> But hey, if people dont wanna spend time and energy explaining it up me, thats totally fair. I welcomed people to ignore me, if they didn't feel like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:49:12-07:00","id":668548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=668511#post668511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> Also, nice going there, dredging up an old arguement. That was totally nessesary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those who forget history are doomed to repeat it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, briefly back on topic. Since I was little, I never really felt like I understood most people, so I started joking about being an alien. The more people I've encountered, the more alien I've felt because people seem to make less and less sense to me every year.<br /> <br /> So, I am a Martian. How about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-17-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:06:36-07:00","id":668725,"title":"","content":"This is why we can't have nice things. *points to a baseball and a broken window, glass bedazzling the floor like a denim jacket fresh from 1986*<br /> <br /> Explanations and shit, eh? Good thing I'm so fucking eloquent. I got this one y'all.<br /> Lemme preface this by saying I know two things extremely well, at an almost doctoral level: Jack and Shit but what I've experienced or read places. Don't be too impressed. Got that almost-degree in Tijuana for a buck.<br /> _________________________________________________<br /> <br /> Alright, so let's cut the crap. There seems to be some confusion between beliefs, feelings and the concept of body image here. Let's take that knot apart first. As I've said, I only speak from personal experience and a random assortment of Google searches over the years.<br /> <br /> Body image, and especially one's internal/imaginary image of their outer self. I'm not talking about how you'd like to have a certain feature because it's sexually attractive, popularly connected with a certain aesthetic or what have you. I'm talking about that image, which often grows a bit right along with you, of how you *should* look. Not because you want it, but because it's just how you look without significant injury or a clown mask or something. Only instead it's like having a phantom limb without the interesting story about how you lost it. And sometimes that phantom limb that twinges every now and again is your entire being.<br /> Desire for change comes after in my story. It began with me noticing that I felt incomplete. I'll start with the claws. I grew up with animals. Mostly cats. Nothing much to add beyond &quot;hung out with cats sometimes&quot;, but it's possibly relevant background information, so whatever. I would look at them clawing at furniture and feel like that was a natural thing for me to do as well. I was literate by age three, so I was already understanding certain basic concepts: the stove is hot, don't wander off unattended (didn't really respect that one..) and, it almost went without saying, you're not a fucking cat, Joey.<br /> That did NOT stop me from nuzzling things that were soft and pushing over heavy furniture because I couldn't seem to get my non-existent claws into the fabric.<br /> In elementary school, I was often picked on for being the chubby quiet one who read a lot, so I got into fights. Little fighting background: my father is insane. Not clinically, he just decided to raise a cage fighter without consulting literally anything beyond the movie Bloodsport. His favorite bonding activity was exercise that could make you shit your pants and then punching an Everlast heavy-bag until my mom eventually found where we were and dinner happened, immediately followed by a martial arts movie and a little exercise.<br /> This is a derail of a derail now, but the fact that I'm still fat after that is fucking aggravating. Just saying. My point here is, I knew how to throw a punch growing up. Despite that, all those fights were mostly me clawing, snarling and biting. That makes sense to me because, when I let myself just relax and picture myself being, I can swear that my teeth are sharper, that my arms are a little longer and that there are dark, almost sooty claws about an inch or two long at the ends of my digits. Toes too. This goes doubly for the wings that I feel I have, at least inside. They're a soft amalgam of avian and chiropteran characteristics, articulated a lot like an oddly distended hand, but lightly feathered in black, like a farm crow.<br /> <br /> Now that I've said that, I suppose I should address mental illness. I'll start by saying I am diagnosed with some. I refuse to lie about that to bolster this explanation. I have bipolar disorder, post-traumatic stress disorder and generalized anxiety disorder. I'm also in the process of being examined for suspected high-functioning autism. In order; a chemical imbalance impacting my mood and decision making, a trauma based disorder that causes major depressive episodes along with easily triggered scares and survival type behavior that's accompanied by being nervous and kinda scared in general. And I just might have trouble with interpersonal skills for a reason beyond being a dork. None of that seems to fit the body image stuff, unless there's an &quot;I totally have wings&quot; mood I'm unaware of that isn't caused by Red Bull.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> Let's move to feelings and beliefs! I'm torn about religion. It often irks, mostly chafes, and I sometimes just go with it anyway. I often don't. When I am feeling religious, I get rather eclectic. A little Shinto-esque ritual animism and ancestor worship, a little Catholicism, a touch of random ideas that are helping me emotionally and spiritually. It varies sometimes. Again, most of this doesn't really inform how I SEE myself, BUT, it might give background to the vampiric part of me, the predator. Granted, so could the beat em ups, but we covered that. Anyway, I do believe in &quot;life energy&quot; and the spirit or soul. I do see my soul as my inner self, so I expect what I see in me to be what the spirit world sees. What God sees, even.<br /> I also Feel as though that soul, the self in myself, is hungry for crap I can't buy at the supermarket. It's partly why I'm chunky, too. I'm literally never not hungry. I can always eat. I've been told I was &quot;eating my feelings&quot; before, but I've checked and I'm pretty sure even MOMENTARY satisfaction occurs sometimes when people do that. Not me. I like certain food, but when I'm hungry I'm like a human tapeworm. I can just go until my body starts rejecting, and it's never made me feel satisfactorily full. I've been checked for neurological disorders that might cause bouts of hunger like that. Nothing so far.<br /> I've also eaten a tiny handful of live bugs. Many times, which is why I wasn't bug-specific. Worms, moths, certain spiders. I've eaten many a crawling thing. And every time I've felt so much better. Like I just had a relaxing meal with a light massage after. I've tried it with dead bugs, too. Nothing but a slightly over FDA approval-level mouthful of insect fragments. I found out later that I could get that same refueling feeling from certain interactions with living things, mostly predatory animals and people in certain moods, but also certain plants even.<br /> It wasn't until I was a teen that I discovered Real Vampire culture, and sanguine feeding (for now, I'll just say my friends were willing to invest time in my ideas regardless of how weird they sounded) which was just before I bought my first copy of VtM.<br /> <br /> \u200b I kinda discovered tabletop by accident. I wanted to know more about Real vamps. Were they like me? I got on message boards, chat rooms. Anything to understand what the hell was so different about me. I felt it and not understanding sucked.<br /> It was on an old site called Pathway to Darkness and its forum that finally gave me some answers. About vampirism AND my more bestial Otherkin traits.<br /> I found people that had simple explanations for why I was so goddamn hungry all the time, and so tired even though I hated sleeping at night and even why I got upset sometimes when I didn't see the moon. (Also, thanks for telling me about VtM, Anna aka MorgueAnna, wherever you are. Totally didn't eat my social life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) I can't regurgitate everything I've learned in one post, but I hope this is a decent start. I'll go on. Need clarification or a deeper explanation, I'll try to provide one. I'm still learning about myself, too, as I suppose all people are to one degree or another, so this definitely isn't the last word.<br /> <br /> Hey, can we try not to argue without merit to the conversation topic here?<br /> Just asking, hoping against hope. Maybe if we try to behave, we can actually attempt understanding.<br /> <br /> Later masturbators,<br /> \u200bAz.<br /> Edit: A bear AND a Martian? Does that mean in the DC Earth Prime universe your weakness is flaming marshmallows from campgrounds? Now I'm curious..<br /> <br /> Edit2: Christ, that sounded flippant. My apologies, PB. Martian specifically, or just alien in general? Please, go on. I'm genuinely curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-17-2015, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:48:45-07:00","id":668768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=668725#post668725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: A bear AND a Martian? Does that mean in the DC Earth Prime universe your weakness is flaming marshmallows from campgrounds? Now I'm curious..<br /> <br /> Edit2: Christ, that sounded flippant. My apologies, PB. Martian specifically, or just alien in general? Please, go on. I'm genuinely curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the gag started, it was Martian. Why? Just because. That &quot;Men are form Mars...&quot; book wasn't even out at the time. I don't subscribe fully to any version of Martian I've seen in popular culture. I just made up my own as I went along. If I could shapeshift and read minds like J'onn J'onzz, I'd love it. I don't think I'd care to be any of John Carter's Martians.<br /> <br /> The bear stuff came later with a lot of the shamanism exploration. In part, it was a mantle thrust upon me. The person who first got my interested in alt beliefs kinda went off the deep end with rage and blaming other for his failures, so he really didn't have the right to it anymore. Whether he realizes he handed it off to me or not, I don't know because I haven't spoken to him since. It's settled in more and more over the years until I fully embraced it. I kind of had to after a vision of a bear and a long conversation with him one Halloween night.<br /> <br /> I still feel very detached from humanity, either way. Today, I'm definitely feeling it. Very off in my own headspace with no obvious paths out.<br /> <br /> And no, flaming marshmallows will not make me run and hide. They're nummy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T08:19:49-07:00","id":669722,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">S\u200bince it appears to need to be said again,, arguing with moderators and their directions, even via PM, is grounds for suspension or permanent revocation of posting privileges. If you disagree with a moderator's directive you are to use the Admin contact information and comply with said directive unless/until informed otherwise by an admin. Being an Iconoclast/free thinker gives no special protection from the forum rules of behavior.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-18-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:10:01-07:00","id":669974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to ask you some stuff too, arc n pb. Remind me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask thru any channel you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:54:33-07:00","id":670132,"title":"","content":"I typed up a long as fuck post then accidently hit the back button on my phone T_T<br /> <br /> Long story short caues fuck all if i'm typing it all up again.<br /> <br /> I dont know what resides in my soul, I've always been that person who laughed at the otherkin stuff to be &quot;normal&quot; but really kinda thought perhaps it made sense to me as to why i dont feel like my body is mine. I've pushed it back for years ignoring it, only in hte last year or so have i allowed myself to even begin to embrace that side of myself whatever it may be. I'm a little umcomfortable saying more now, i'm kinda glad the back button ate my post..My fiance if he saw my original post would never let me hear the end of it and laugh his fucking ass off at me, in fact his comments related to otherkin make me wanna punch him(same views he has on transgender people needless to say NOT good), so i just dont ever get the chance to talk about it, and talking is a massive way that i sort my brain out and figure things out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 09-18-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:53:41-07:00","id":670209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=670132#post670132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I typed up a long as fuck post then accidently hit the back button on my phone T_T<br /> Long story short caues fuck all if i'm typing it all up again.<br /> I dont know what resides in my soul, I've always been that person who laughed at the otherkin stuff to be &quot;normal&quot; but really kinda thought perhaps it made sense to me as to why i dont feel like my body is mine. I've pushed it back for years ignoring it, only in hte last year or so have i allowed myself to even begin to embrace that side of myself whatever it may be. I'm a little umcomfortable saying more now, i'm kinda glad the back button ate my post..My fiance if he saw my original post would never let me hear the end of it and laugh his fucking ass off at me, in fact his comments related to otherkin make me wanna punch him(same views he has on transgender people needless to say NOT good), so i just dont ever get the chance to talk about it, and talking is a massive way that i sort my brain out and figure things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, post it anyway. We'll listen. And ignore the others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:38:50-07:00","id":670343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=670209#post670209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, post it anyway. We'll listen. And ignore the others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded heartily!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:13:05-07:00","id":670356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=669974#post669974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask thru any channel you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto.<br /> <br /> Not the Pokemon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:30:26-07:00","id":670532,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Arc and PB. That's thoughtful of you. <br /> I'm sure asking either one of you would greatly expand my thinking in certain ways.<br /> <br /> I'd really love it if we could get a public dialogue about Otherkin going here.<br /> <br /> I'll share something new that happened literally just this last morning:<br /> <br /> I explained my Otherkin identity to my mom today, in detail. How much detail? Read my previous posts. She did. After deciding that it seemed easier to digest in text format, I &quot;came out&quot; as Vampire/Otherkin to my mother by letting her read exactly what you have. Just MY posts. After that we talked about it.<br /> <br /> She was confused. She was a little worried. We eventually got to talking about my childhood and some off my early precursor characteristics. <br /> <br /> I can honestly say I was able to explain both psy, ambient and sanguine feeding to my mom, without awkwardness. And...she got it. She actually understood what I meant. The explanation I gave her involved an example of me touching a tree to lightly feed. I explained WHAT I did, but not the process.<br /> <br /> She replied by knitting her eyebrows and admitting she'd done almost the very same before. She just hadn't seen it that way. <br /> <br /> Progress? I think so. I mean, the woman accepts the fact I have wings.<br /> <br /> Thanks for being you, Mom. I'm more than grateful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:48:55-07:00","id":671164,"title":"","content":"Congratulations, AZ! It is great to have family that will try their best to understand you, and supports you wether they fully understand or not.<br /> <br /> I love this community, so I'm going to take a risk here and express something pretty personal. I wouldn't say that I identify as Otherkin, but I do empathize strongly with the feeling of being something else in human skin. It's not so much as you describe, AZ, feeling like your body is supposed to be different than it is. More that I feel no connection to my body at all. It's like my body is <i>where</i> I am, but not <i>what</i> I am, the same way I'm not my house just because I live inside it.<br /> <br /> I've read about people experiencing dissociation, and the way I've seen it described sounds almost exactly like the way I feel, except that from what I've read it's usually a temporary feeling, and a response to abuse or trauma. But I've had this feeling all my life, and I had a very happy childhood, I've never been abused, and I don't think the trauma I have experienced in my life has been especially severe. Besides, I very much enjoy this feeling, whereas it sounds like most people who dissociate find it very distressing.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I think this feeling of disconnect from my physical body might be part of the reason I've never felt dysmorphia related to my gender identity. My body doesn't feel like mine in the first place, so how could it be &quot;wrong&quot;? It's just the vessel I need in order to exist in and interact with the world around me, why would I care what sexual organs it has?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T12:09:19-07:00","id":671177,"title":"","content":"Curious, I feel something similar Charlaquin. When trying to explain it I usually use a car as an example, I'm not my car just because I'm inside it and move around in it. The body is something similar. Also, no distress at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:01:16-07:00","id":671225,"title":"","content":"Charlaqiun and Thorbes: if you haven't seen it before, you might want to check up on Cartesian Dualism. It's pretty much what you're describing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:02:59-07:00","id":671226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=671177#post671177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious, I feel something similar Charlaquin. When trying to explain it I usually use a car as an example, I'm not my car just because I'm inside it and move around in it. The body is something similar. Also, no distress at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Glad to know I'm not alone in feeling that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:31:06-07:00","id":671468,"title":"","content":"Okay i can finally post again had to wait til li could get to my laptop cause i'm so done with posting from my cell phone. and my finace I found out doesnt come to this fourm any more so WIN.<br /> <br /> If this seems confusing sorry i'm just going to type as my thoughts cross my mind and pray for not being judged. (hillarious cause i'll stand in front of a walmart and take off my clothes(it was hot out, walked home in a bra and underwear cause fuck what everyone else thinks i was dying lol but oooh talk about the depths of my soul? shit i better hide!)<br /> <br /> For as long as I can remember I have never felt right in my body, I felt deep down i was something else, i attributed it to my lovely mental issues, and pushed it aside cause mental issues are one thing believeing you are in the wrong body is a whole nother thing. As i got stable that feeling never went away, in fact it only got stronger and the dreams from my guide only got stronger as he urged me to accept myself and to embrace who I am and what I am. <br /> <br /> But what am I? My guide is a dick, and wont give me the answer, only says he will give me the tools and lead me towards finding it out but wont outright tell me shit. My guide as i refer to him has no name he's a crow I know that, i've seen him in my dreams as both an actual crow and a hauntingly beautiful pale man with black wings and white skin, I'm not that crazy i dont see or hear him when i'm awake, he comes to me in my dreams or when i mediate and reach out to him for guidance. <br /> <br /> I feel like my body is clunky and wrong, theres an animal in my soul, my desire to run (in the physical sense, i want to runnnnn always run, but my body is to weak to tolerate it.) I'm a meat eater for the most part I WONT go near veggies, the taste the texture its all wrong, wheres the blood, wheres that beautiful taste that comes with a piece of meat? I've never been afraid of falling nor heights i love the feeling of looking down on thr world from a high point its an exiliaration I love.<br /> <br /> I hate staying in one place long I always feel like tying myself down to a place is wrong. But money keeps moving impossible so I do what i can to satisfy that by moving things around my house and making it feel &quot;new&quot;. I get &quot;homesick&quot; so much it hurts but i dont know where the fuck home is, and i'm searching for it, maybe one day i'll find it. I came close when i went up the gorge, the woods, the high cliffs the water. (OOh water how i love it, not to drink...Its the only time my homesickness fades by about 95%, its so freeing and calm.) Like az i feel a closeness to the moon, i KNOW when its full without ever stepping outside. Me during a full moon = a rage filled mess my WORST and most violent mood swing used to happen around the full moon, to the point one i realized this i'd make sure to take steps to calm myself or go the fuck to sleep before the sun set and the moon rose.<br /> <br /> This will sound so fucking insane but I feel like i should fly, when i'm tense or anxious and want to flee i feel a tensness in my shoulders where wings would sit that makes my flex my shoulder blades to ease the tension though it doesnt go away. I cant stretch my wings and fly, this body simply isnt meant for that. <br /> <br /> For many years I shut this shit down locked it up in my mind the best i could to avoid it as talking about it would get me told i'm nuts, and that its wrong. (would it have been less wrong had i felt i was man? maybe, thats more easy to accept then saying i feel in my soul i am not human at all.) The longer i denied it the stronger my dreams, and the more i was urged to stop repressing it because it was bad for my well being to deny who i am. If i embrace it and accept it, i'll feel better i may not be able to fly BUT I have things to learn that only a humans perspective can learn. This cycle of my life is important, I am an animal but what kind i dont know and it will require I allow my mind even more right to roam and listen to my guide to uncover something i've repressed for so long and locked behind many walls and barriers. <br /> <br /> I also am a mother. To deny a part of myself would make me a hypocrite when i tell my daughter that she should accept who she is and fuck what anyone else says or thinks of it, because its what she feels that matters. Why is it so hard for me to follow that same guideline?<br /> <br /> I feel like i sound insane talking aobut being an animal in soul on a journey to learn something from a human life...this is seriously the first time i've ever spoken of it cause fuck if if i'd mentioned it to my therapist the look i'd imagine she'd give me would be that of judgement as she writes up a referral for stronger medication.<br /> <br /> Oddly over the last year and a half as i started to stop denying it bit by bit i've felt better more &quot;me&quot;. I still have a ways to go though before i understand it and many walls to tear down to uncover the truth. I never realzied i could build walls in my mind that were strong enough i couldnt easily drop them again, but then again, maybe i'm still hesitating?<br /> <br /> I'm second guessing myself in hitting post. this has sat typed up for the last ten minuets as i stared at it debating on whether or not i should even post this rambling from my brain that in all honesty makes me sound batshit crazy. I believe in the supernatural, ghosts, magic, psychics, other supernatural beings, past lives, many gods and god, i believe in reincarnation and that each life is a lesson. am i insane?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:34:22-07:00","id":671528,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say you're insane. Your experience doesn't really fit in my world-view, but that's a limitation of me rather than an aberration of you.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing, I'll do my best to understand it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T16:58:29-07:00","id":672498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=671528#post671528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for sharing, I'll do my best to understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the world heard this sentence more, I think it'd be a better place. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T23:28:40-07:00","id":672950,"title":"","content":"Thank you for sharing, Scel. It was so comforting to read that the physical tension I feel from not being able to use or flex my bestial features like my wings or just the tightness in my wrists from the retractable claws I can never stretch isn't just me being weird.<br /> <br /> That was brave of you and I want to thank you for being honest. I respect and appreciate you actually hitting post.<br /> <br /> <br /> The part about your carnivorous nature really hit home.<br /> I'm a TINY bit different in that respect, mainly only because I've had a while to process that my hunger isn't necessarily in my stomach, so I tolerate veggies for the nutrients sometimes. Learning about my hunger has helped a lot. I still really miss sanguine feeding though. Few ways are as satisfying.<br /> I say few, not none.<br /> <br /> On that note, I was feeling physically awful when I woke up and managed to make myself feel WAY better by a consensual psionic feeding from a long-lived and spiritually strong plant. Yes. I asked the plant first. The plant was nice enough to let me have some energy to fix myself up. If you'd have seen me, it would have looked like me holding hands with my great-grandmother's decorative heirloom vine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://awakeanddrink.org/?subpages=psionics&amp;pages=psifeeding\" target=\"_blank\">http://awakeanddrink.org/?subpages=p...ges=psifeeding</a><br /> <br /> Here's a link to a VERY basic explanation of psionic feeding from someone other than myself. I don't really have much of a visualization process when feeding, which the author of the article describes and I've had described to me often. Feeding for me very much involves a &quot;gut feeling&quot; or rudimentary sixth sense maybe in how I sense energy sources and attach to them. I've used visualization extensively, but I'm an imaginative person anyway, so when things get visceral I sort of just tune that that out to avoid distractions. I could very well be manifesting &quot;tentacles&quot; in my feeding process that I'm just unaware of.<br /> \u200b I understand ambient feeding and feeding from a distance, and have used that in the past. So far, it's still much easier and more enjoyable to include some physical proximity or contact when feeding, however.<br /> <br /> I really don't know how much of a dialogue we're having here yet, so please feel free to just ask random questions to me specifically, if you'd like to know something particular. If it's TOO personal, I'll let you know. I'm choosing to be extremely open here in support of fellow people who may identify as Otherkin, Vampire, Lycanthrope*, psychically sensitive, Fae, hybrid, alien, Youkai or anything else that could be called Other. We're here. We're real. I'm a person. I'm also a Vampire. And a winged anthropomorphic lycanthrope. I'm not completely unique in this situation.<br /> That means there are people out there, just as real as myself, who can't tell the people around them simple things, like How They Feel, What They Think or Who/What They Are. That really sucks.<br /> <br /> Some safety for them (us) to be honest would be nice.<br /> <br /> - Az<br /> <br /> * <a href=\"http://otherkin.wikia.com/wiki/Lycanthropy\" target=\"_blank\">http://otherkin.wikia.com/wiki/Lycanthropy</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-22-2015, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:31:21-07:00","id":676169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=672950#post672950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for sharing, Scel. It was so comforting to read that the physical tension I feel from not being able to use or flex my bestial features like my wings or just the tightness in my wrists from the retractable claws I can never stretch isn't just me being weird.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> still kinda sideeyeing my own post but hey whatever!<br /> <br /> Nah its not you being &quot;Weird&quot; at all! We are missing a part of ourselves in this body and we know it.<br /> <br /> On the carnivorus thing:<br /> I dont see how you tolerate them even for nutrients, I keep trying cause yano its good to be in good health, but fuck all if i can do it...On the upside clearly i dont need them, all my blood panels are coming back actually more then okay for nutrient levels and shit so TAKE THAT VEGGIES i dont need you to be a healthy adult...(though i may need you so i dont spend forever fat...Or yano i could just get off my ass and put down the cookies that would work too lol)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm actually quite curious about the psychic feeding thing, its not something i do, or even thought of doing but the whole idea is interesting to read about. Hillariously my finace did in fact see this, and his response was, hey you know you feed off rage right? Every time we fight, you steal my energy, but are always invigorated yourself afterwards. I laughed my ass off, cause i dont think that way at all, to me its just once i vent I feel less tired, him being tired is just cause he has to put up with me XDD Of course this is the same man who read exalted and said he finally figured out what i was a Fair folk...I took that as an insult at first, then just giggled and agreed cause well he's not ALL wrong. (Not saying i'm a fae just saying what a complete not understanding person thinks i am) He says i need to man up and realize i'm a not an animal but if he believed in this kind of stuff he'd say I was one of the fae.<br /> <br /> Surprisingly he didnt make fun of me, but he did admit he doesnt believe in this kind of stuff and thinks its weird/a mental ilness that i or anyone else thinks this way. grrr. well at least he's not being a dick about it...probably cause he KNEW i'd punch him in the nuts if he was.<br /> Oh and his version of understanding after reading this was to start in on saying how much we should play Beast the primordial ;&gt;&gt; *Facepalm*<br /> <br /> AZ, I do infact have a question when you feed off another person not at a distance do you touch them? Does it leave the otehr person tired or feeling different(if you ever asked them that is). Why is touch an important factor? OOhh and on the topic of sanguine feeding, isnt it hard to find someone willing to allow that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 09-24-2015, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T01:31:51-07:00","id":676170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=671528#post671528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say you're insane. Your experience doesn't really fit in my world-view, but that's a limitation of me rather than an aberration of you.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing, I'll do my best to understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm seconded Az on this one, seriously need more people like you in the world","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T03:27:47-07:00","id":676266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/666688-the-otherkin-thread?p=676169#post676169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> still kinda sideeyeing my own post but hey whatever!<br /> <br /> Nah its not you being &quot;Weird&quot; at all! We are missing a part of ourselves in this body and we know it.<br /> <br /> On the carnivorus thing:<br /> I dont see how you tolerate them even for nutrients, I keep trying cause yano its good to be in good health, but fuck all if i can do it...On the upside clearly i dont need them, all my blood panels are coming back actually more then okay for nutrient levels and shit so TAKE THAT VEGGIES i dont need you to be a healthy adult...(though i may need you so i dont spend forever fat...Or yano i could just get off my ass and put down the cookies that would work too lol<br /> <br /> AZ, I do infact have a question when you feed off another person not at a distance do you touch them? Does it leave the otehr person tired or feeling different(if you ever asked them that is). Why is touch an important factor? OOhh and on the topic of sanguine feeding, isnt it hard to find someone willing to allow that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I basically just shovel the vegetables into my face like drinking Nyquil. It's gross, but I need fiber. One exception; if I eat something off a live plant like a flower or a leaf of something, it's fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feeding up close: I usually touch my donor/source. Imagine that I visualize energy like electricity. If I'm directly connected, then the energy doesn't need to arc and can more easily flow without interruption. It just makes feeding easier.<br /> <br /> It very often leaves the donor feeling tired or drained in some fashion afterward, but usually they're on board with the good and bad of the process. If they're NOT, maybe one shouldn't be feeding on them. I make it a point not to feed on someone sick or emotionally drained to avoid possibly worsening their condition or health. Some people are natural energy creators, like the reverse of a Vampire. These people often, if into it, make excellent donors and sometimes report being able to have calmer days and nights.<br /> <br /> As for sanguine feeding, I haven't done it in years, not counting some mostly symbolic autovampirism (drinking my own blood) that a close and intimate friend decided she needed a buddy for. At one point, when I was sexually active, it was a little hardcore in a razor and bloody lips kinda way. It's ALWAYS hard to find someone interested and willing. There are whole message boards and subforums dedicated to donors and their patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-24-2015, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","va